---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>State Trackr</h1>
			<p>
				For Informational Purposes Only. State Trackr is an independent platform 
				built to make staying informed about your state's legislative action simple 
				and accessible. We believe civic engagement shouldn't be hard to find.
			</p>
			<p>
				<section style="background: #1e293b; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 2rem; border: 1px solid #334155;">
				<h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">A Note From State Trackr</h2>
				<p>State Trackr currently updates once a week on Sunday nights. All updates are typically completed by Monday morning.</p>
				<p>State Trackr is in Beta, so you'll see constant tweaks as I find the best way to present this data. Whether you want to see more info or less, your input helps shape the app.</p>
				<p>Reach out anytime at: <strong>contact@statetrackr.com</strong></p>
			</section>

			<section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
				<h2>Data Transparency</h2>
				<p>
					All legislative data is sourced through <strong>LegiScan</strong>, which monitors current legislative action across the board. While State Trackr holds the deepest respect for our veterans and those who have achieved great things for our country, we’ve chosen to filter ceremonial bills (like the naming of roads or bridges) so that major legislative actions don’t get drowned out.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
